Admin promotion routes are `/shop/admin/promotions` (GET list, GET `/:id`, POST create, PUT `/:id` update), `PATCH /:id/status`, POST `/:id/archive`, POST `/:id/restore`, and GET `/:id/usage`. They are restricted to admin, super_admin, and manager. Create/update accept `name`, `code`, `description`, `type`, `status`, `priority`, `startAt`, `endAt`, `usageLimit`, `perCustomerLimit`, `percent`, `fixedAmount`, `minOrderAmount`, `maxDiscountAmount`, `applicableProducts`, `applicableVariants`, `applicableCategories`, `excludedProducts`, `excludedVariants`, `excludedCategories`, `excludedSaleItems`, `eligibleCustomerIds`, `firstOrderOnly`, `stackable`, `exclusive`, `maxApplicablePerOrder`, `shippingThreshold`, `requireCode`, `triggeredByCode`, and `bogo`. Supported types are `PERCENTAGE`, `FIXED_AMOUNT`, `COUPON`, `AUTOMATIC`, `FIRST_ORDER`, `PRODUCT`, `CATEGORY`, `CUSTOMER_SPECIFIC`, `BOGO`, `BUNDLE`, and `FREE_SHIPPING`; statuses are `draft`, `active`, `paused`, `expired`, and `archived`. Codes are normalized to uppercase and may contain only letters, digits, `_`, and `-`; names must be at least 2 characters. Percent is 0–100; amounts and limits must be non-negative; dates must be ordered; BOGO quantities must be positive/non-negative as applicable. Type-specific required configuration is validated before use. Status accepts `{ "status": "..." }` and follows explicit transition rules; archive and restore are lifecycle operations, not hard deletion. Mutation responses use `{ success: true, promotion }`, while usage returns `{ success: true, usage }`.

Financial reports are mounted at `/shop/admin/reports`: `GET /revenue`, `/products`, `/customers`, `/customers/:customerId/history`, `/creators`, `/conversions`, `/promotions`, and `/export.csv`. `/revenue`, `/customers`, `/customers/:customerId/history`, `/promotions`, and `/export.csv` require admin, super_admin, manager, or finance. `/products`, `/creators`, and `/conversions` also allow creators and vendors; creator/vendor results are scoped to the caller's own creator ID. CSV export returns a file rather than a JSON envelope.

## Error behavior

Validation errors generally return HTTP 400 with either `{ error: "Validation failed", details: [{ field, message }] }` or `{ success: false, error }`. Unauthorized requests return 401/403; missing catalog/order records return 404. Checkout uses 409 for conflicting idempotency, ownership, or stock states. Uploads return 413 above the 100 MiB application limit. Unhandled errors use `{ success: false, error, correlationId }`.
